&gt;
At Woolpert, you&#x27;ll do work that matters.
&gt;
As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you&#x27;ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
Position Overview
&gt;
Seeking a new career challenge? Then Woolpert is seeking you! Woolpert is hiring a Survey Intern to join our Survey and Geospatial team for the 2027 internship program . This full-time internship provides students with the opportunity to gain hands-on experience supporting field and office surveying operations while working alongside experienced survey professionals on a variety of infrastructure, transportation, aviation, utility, and geospatial projects.
&gt;
As a Survey Intern, you will assist with collecting, processing, and analyzing survey data that supports engineering design, construction, mapping, asset management, and community development initiatives. You may contribute to boundary and topographic surveys, control surveys, mobile and terrestrial laser scanning, UAV support operations, GIS data collection, transportation asset inventories, and other geospatial projects that directly impact the communities where we live and work.
&gt;
This intern will be a full-time position for both field and office operations out of multiple locations with opportunities to travel. Woolpert does not provide relocation assistance for interns.
&gt;
Woolpert is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Applicants must already possess authorization to work in the country where this position is located.
&gt;
What You Will Do
&gt;
Work as an integral member of a survey field crew and project team.
&gt;
Assist licensed surveyors, survey technicians, and geospatial professionals with field data collection activities.
&gt;
Operate and learn advanced surveying…

Your Impact at LILA
&gt;
This PhD-level co-op will join the Life Science AI team to contribute to applied ML research in protein engineering, including generative protein design, antibody engineering, developability, and wet-lab-informed model iteration. Working alongside Lila scientists and ML researchers, the co-op will explore generative and predictive models for protein sequence, structure, and function, analyze biological and experimental datasets to evaluate model outputs, and prototype workflows that connect model predictions, candidate prioritization, and wet-lab feedback. Results will be communicated through code, notebooks, written summaries, and presentations.
&gt;
The ideal candidate is a currently enrolled PhD student in CS, ML, computational biology, bioengineering, biophysics, or a related field, with research experience in ML or protein engineering, strong Python skills, and experience with frameworks like PyTorch or JAX. Familiarity with protein language models, diffusion or flow-based models, antibody design, or active learning workflows is a plus.
&gt;
The role advances our domain-specific protein design models while the data, methods, and evaluation tools built along the way also strengthen our general AI research model, directly supporting Lila&#x27;s mission of combining automated data generation with scientific superintelligence.
&gt;
What You&#x27;ll Be Building
&gt;
Research generative and predictive models for protein and antibody design
&gt;
Analyze experimental datasets to evaluate model outputs and guide design decisions
&gt;
Prototype workflows linking model predictions, candidate prioritization, and wet-lab feedback
&gt;
Build datasets and benchmarks that support both domain-specific and general AI research models
&gt;
Share results through code, notebooks, and presentations
&gt;
What You&#x27;ll Need to Succeed
&gt;
Currently enrolled PhD student in CS, ML, computational biology, bioengineering, biophysics, or a related field
&gt;
Research experience in machine learning,…

Who we are
&gt;
About Stripe
&gt;
Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies-from the world&#x27;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups-use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#x27;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.
&gt;
About the teams
&gt;
Stripe&#x27;s Controllership organization is responsible for the accurate and timely recording of Stripe&#x27;s business activities, the integrity of our financial reporting, and the scalable processes and controls that support our growth. We partner across Finance, Product, Engineering, Operations, Sales, Legal, Tax, Treasury, and Internal Audit to understand Stripe&#x27;s products and operations, resolve complex financial issues, and maintain a strong control environment.
&gt;
We are hiring four Controllership Interns, with one role on each of the following teams: Accounts Receivable (AR), Controls, Product Accounting, and Corporate Accounting. In any placement, you&#x27;ll work with experienced teammates and cross-functional partners on meaningful accounting, data, systems, controls, or process-improvement work.
&gt;
Accounts Receivable (AR) supports invoicing, collections, cash application, and related financial operations through scalable, accurate, and auditable processes.
&gt;
Controls supports Stripe&#x27;s internal-control environment by documenting and assessing processes, identifying risks, supporting control testing, and helping teams design sustainable improvements.
&gt;
Product Accounting supports Stripe&#x27;s products by understanding their financial-data flows, evaluating accounting implications, and developing scalable processes
&gt;
Corporate Accounting supports Stripe&#x27;s close, financial reporting, corporate accounting processes, and control…

Who we are
&gt;
Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected OperationsTM Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing - and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.
&gt;
Working at Samsara means you&#x27;ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that&#x27;s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you&#x27;ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.
&gt;
&gt; About the role
&gt;
As a Security Operations Engineer at Samsara, you will join a global team dedicated to protecting our people, systems, and information. You will triage and investigate security alerts, run incident response efforts, and help improve the tools, runbooks, and automated workflows we use to detect and respond to threats.
&gt;
This role is an ideal next step if you have built foundational experience in a SOC or hands-on security environment and want to develop your technical craft. At Samsara, we view this level as a collaborative apprenticeship: you will develop independent execution skills on discrete investigations, break down incoming alerts into actionable steps, partner with incident stakeholders to remediate findings, and work alongside experienced responders during complex security incidents. You will also explore modern AI tools and insights to simplify routine tasks and optimize your day-to-day workflow.
&gt;
We are…

